      "name": "HashStringELF",
      "signature": "uint HashStringELF(char * szKey, uint dwTableSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Computes ELF hash of a string and returns result modulo table size.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize hash to 0\n2. For each char: hash = (hash << 4) + char\n3. If high nibble set, XOR with high bits shifted down\n4. Return hash % dwTableSize\n\nParameters:\n- szKey (char*): Null-terminated string to hash\n- dwTableSize (uint): Hash table size for modulo\n\nReturns:\n- Hash value in range [0, dwTableSize-1]\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF0000000: High nibble mask\n- 0x0FFFFFFF: Low 28-bit mask\n- 0x18 (24): Shift for high nibble extraction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ae8c633c90b73d006aec157749a6f0a5",
