      "name": "LookupStringInHashTable",
      "signature": "uint LookupStringInHashTable(byte * pStringTable, int * pHashTable, byte * pbKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Looks up a string key in a hash table and returns its string index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute ELF hash of pbKey string\n2. Hash modulo bucket count gives starting slot\n3. Linear probe through slots until match or exhausted\n4. Compare stored key against pbKey at each occupied slot\n5. If match found, store index value and return slot info\n\nParameters:\n- pStringTable (byte*): Pointer to string table header struct\n  - offset 0x02: ushort - name table name count\n  - offset 0x04: uint - hash bucket count\n  - offset 0x0D: uint - max probe iterations\n  - offset 0x15+: hash slots (16 bytes each)\n- pHashTable (int*): Parallel array of string indices per bucket\n- pbKey (byte*): Null-terminated key string to look up\n\nReturns:\n- Low word: String index (1-based) or 0xFFFF if not found\n- High word: Additional slot data\n\nHash Slot Layout (16 bytes):\n- byte at +0: Status (1 = occupied)\n- int at +7: Offset to key string within table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Hash slot size (16 bytes)\n- 0xF0000000: ELF hash high bits mask\n- 0x18: ELF hash right shift (24 bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:c2a87e88cc39d47d07be4676c549d45e",
