      "name": "UnloadStringTable",
      "signature": "void UnloadStringTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decrements string table reference count and frees all resources when zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if base string table is loaded, exit early if not\n2. Decrement reference count; exit if still in use\n3. Free base hash table (0x340) and string data (0x345)\n4. Free base string table (0x12d)\n5. Free patch hash table (0x353) and string data (0x358)\n6. Free patch string table (0x12d)\n7. Free expansion hash table (0x361) and string data (0x366)\n8. Free expansion string table (0x12d)\n9. Walk and free untranslated cache linked list (0x3a0, 0x3a1, 0x3a2 per node)\n10. Call unloadSysMap to release system character mapping\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12d (301): String table pool ID\n- 0x340 (832): Base hash table pool ID\n- 0x345 (837): Base string data pool ID\n- 0x353 (851): Patch hash table pool ID\n- 0x358 (856): Patch string data pool ID\n- 0x361 (865): Expansion hash table pool ID\n- 0x366 (870): Expansion string data pool ID\n- 0x3a0 (928): Untranslated cache string pool ID\n- 0x3a1 (929): Untranslated cache data pool ID\n- 0x3a2 (930): Untranslated cache node pool ID",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:45754c7defddbafdfef21ae1288d8729",
