      "name": "GetSystemLanguageId",
      "signature": "uint GetSystemLanguageId(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves the system language identifier based on OS platform.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetVersionExA to determine Windows platform type\n2. For Win9x (platform ID 1): Read sLanguage from win.ini [Intl] section\n3. For Win NT (platform ID 2): Read sLanguage from registry HKCU\\Control Panel\\International\n4. Validate registry value length (< 4 chars required)\n5. Compare language code against g_pLangCodeTable (20-byte stride entries)\n6. Return matching language ID from g_adwLangIdTable\n\nParameters:\n- None (no parameters)\n\nReturns:\n- Language identifier (uint) from lookup table on success\n- 0 if OS detection fails, language not found, or registry error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x94 (148): sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA)\n- 0x14 (20): Language table entry stride\n- 0x20019: KEY_QUERY_VALUE | KEY_ENUMERATE_SUB_KEYS | KEY_NOTIFY\n- 0x80000001: HKEY_CURRENT_USER",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
