      "name": "GetLocaleString",
      "signature": "void GetLocaleString(int nStringType, char * szBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Retrieves a locale-specific string based on string type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize locale system on first call (lazy init)\n2. Look up locale ID (0-12) in g_adwLangIdTable to get table index\n3. Based on nStringType, select string pointer from locale table:\n   - 0: Expansion code (e.g. \"ENU\", \"DEU\")\n   - 1: Language code variant\n   - 2: Alternate code\n4. Copy string to szBuffer using inline strlen+memcpy\n\nParameters:\n- nStringType (int): String type selector (0/1/2)\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for locale string\n\nReturns:\n- void (string copied to szBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xD (13): Maximum supported locale ID\n- 0x14 (20): Locale table entry stride (5 DWORDs)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc44882: Locale initialization helper\n- Ordinal_10043: Assert/verify helper",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3c353964c3ef5f6e11a55c507fb7a12f",
