      "name": "IntToUnicodeWithSep",
      "signature": "void IntToUnicodeWithSep(wchar_t * wszBuffer, int nValue, int nMaxLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts an integer to Unicode string with thousand separators (commas).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nMaxLen > 2 (assert fatal via Ordinal_10023 otherwise)\n2. If value is negative, prepend '-' (0x2d) and negate\n3. Convert absolute value to ASCII digit string via FUN_6fc44b1b (itoa base 10)\n4. Calculate output length: strlen + (strlen-1)/3 for comma separators\n5. Write null terminator at calculated output position\n6. Copy digits right-to-left, inserting ',' (0x2c) every 3 digits\n7. If no digits processed, output \"0\" as fallback\n\nParameters:\n- wszBuffer (wchar_t*): Output Unicode buffer for formatted number\n- nValue (int): Signed integer to convert to string\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum buffer length in wchars (must be > 2)\n\nReturns:\n- void (buffer modified in place with null-terminated result)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): Unicode minus sign '-'\n- 0x2c (44): Unicode comma ',' thousand separator\n- 10: Decimal radix for itoa conversion\n- 3: Digits per group for thousand separators\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc44b1b: Integer to ASCII conversion (itoa wrapper)\n- Ordinal_10023: Assertion/error handler (Fog.dll)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
