      "name": "GetBindingState",
      "signature": "uint GetBindingState(void * this, int nCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Get binding state flags for specified binding index, checking against active binding mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare g_dwBindingMode with 1 (check if mode is set)\n2. If mode > 1, call GetBindingStateEx with binding index and flag mask 0x103\n3. Otherwise, look up binding index in g_pBindingStates array (2-byte entries)\n4. Extract state flags using bitmask 0x103 and return\n\nParameters:\n- pThis: This pointer (object context)\n- nBindingIndex: Binding index for lookup (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n- Binding state flags (bitmask 0x103): bit 0 (0x01), bit 1 (0x02), bit 8 (0x100)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Direct array lookup used when g_dwBindingMode <= 1\n- Delegated to GetBindingStateEx when g_dwBindingMode > 1\n- Flag mask 0x103 extracts specific state bits from binding word\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x103: State flag bitmask (0x01 | 0x02 | 0x100)\n- 0x1: Binding mode comparison threshold\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetBindingStateEx() - Extended binding state retrieval (called when mode > 1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:5325db56331a4ad12420901dc1108151",
