      "name": "ConvertIntegerToString",
      "signature": "char * ConvertIntegerToString(dword nValue, char * pszBuffer, dword nRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Convert integer to ASCII string representation in specified base/radix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nValue is negative AND nRadix is 10 (decimal): if yes, set sign flag to 1\n2. If sign flag set, negate nValue to work with absolute value  \n3. Call FUN_6fb9ae1b with nValue, pszBuffer, nRadix, and sign flag\n4. Return pszBuffer pointer\n\nParameters:\ndwValue - Integer value to convert (unsigned)\npszBuffer - Output buffer pointer for ANSI string result\ndwRadix - Base for conversion: 10=decimal, 16=hexadecimal, 8=octal, 2=binary\n\nReturns:\nPointer to output buffer (pszBuffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nRadix is 10 and dwValue is negative (MSB set): prepends minus sign\n- For non-decimal radix: treats value as unsigned regardless of sign bit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x0a (10) - Decimal radix check constant\n0x80000000 (sign bit) - Negative value detection via CMP with 0\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb9ae1b - Core integer-to-string conversion engine with digit generation",
