      "name": "IntToStringRadix",
      "signature": "void IntToStringRadix(uint dwValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwBase, int nNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Convert unsigned integer to string in arbitrary base.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check nNegative flag: if non-zero, write '-' to buffer and negate dwValue\n2. Loop - extract digits by repeated division: dwValue / dwBase (quotient in ESI, remainder in EDX)\n3. Map remainder to character: 0-9 maps to '0'-'9' (add 0x30), 10-35 maps to 'A'-'Z' (add 0x57)\n4. Store digit at szCurrent position and advance pointer\n5. Continue while quotient != 0 (more digits needed)\n6. Null-terminate string after last digit\n7. Reverse entire string by swapping characters from both ends toward middle\n\nParameters:\ndwValue (uint): Value to convert (unsigned, negated if nNegative set)\nszBuffer (char *): Output buffer for string representation\ndwBase (uint): Number base (2-36)\nnNegative (int): Sign flag (if non-zero, prepend '-')\n\nReturns:\nvoid: String written to szBuffer parameter (null-terminated)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c147e94384608ec25ec11bdc009b5d4a",
