      "name": "DisplayRuntimeError",
      "signature": "void DisplayRuntimeError(uint dwErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Displays a CRT runtime error message based on error code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search error table at g_adwRuntimeErrorTable for matching error code\n2. If found and console app (g_dwAppType==1) or error mode is stderr:\n   - Write error string directly to stderr via WriteFile\n3. Else if GUI app and code != 0xFC:\n   - Get module filename (truncate to 60 chars if needed)\n   - Build message: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: <path>\n\n<error msg>\"\n   - Display via FUN_6fc49d1f (MessageBox wrapper)\n\nParameters:\n- dwErrorCode (uint): CRT error code (R6xxx series)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFFF4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH\n- 0x3C (60): Max display length for module path\n- 0xFC (252): Special error code that skips GUI display\n- 0x12010: MB_OK | MB_ICONHAND | MB_TASKMODAL\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc47ab0: String copy helper\n- FUN_6fc47ac0: String concatenate helper\n- FUN_6fc49d1f: MessageBox wrapper",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
