      "name": "AdjustFileBufferBounds",
      "signature": "int AdjustFileBufferBounds(int nRegionBase, int * pnFreeHead, byte * pbBlock, uint dwNewParas)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Attempts to resize a page block in-place for page-based heap allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current block size from first byte of pbBlock\n2. Calculate tracking structure pointer from region base and page offset\n3. If shrinking (dwNewParas < current): update block size, add freed paragraphs to tracker\n4. If expanding: verify target region is within page bounds (0xF8 bytes)\n5. Scan bytes from current end to new end, all must be zero (free)\n6. If scan fails, return 0 (cannot resize in-place)\n7. Update block size byte and adjust free head pointer if expansion overlaps it\n8. Update tracking structure with paragraph delta\n\nParameters:\n- nRegionBase (int): Base address of page heap region\n- pnFreeHead (int*): Pointer to free list head structure ([0]=head ptr, [1]=free count)\n- pbBlock (byte*): Block to resize (first byte = size in paragraphs)\n- dwNewParas (uint): New size in 16-byte paragraphs\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Resize succeeded\n- 0: Cannot resize (no change, exceeds bounds, or non-free bytes in expansion range)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Offset to region base pointer in region structure\n- 0x18 (24): Offset to tracking array in region structure\n- 0xC (12): Page size shift (4096-byte pages)\n- 8: Tracking entry stride\n- 0x3E (62): Max paragraphs per block (248 bytes = 0xF8)\n- 0xF1 (241): Marker value for page tracking state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
