      "name": "ValidateStreamPropertyId",
      "signature": "void ValidateStreamPropertyId(uint dwWinError)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Maps Windows error codes to C runtime errno values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store Windows error in TLS OS error field\n2. Search g_adWinErrToErrnoMap table for exact match\n3. If found, set errno to corresponding mapped value\n4. If not found, check special ranges:\n   - 0x13-0x24: Set errno to EACCES (0xD)\n   - 0xBC-0xCA: Set errno to ENOEXEC (0x8)\n5. Default: Set errno to EINVAL (0x16)\n\nParameters:\n- dwWinError (uint): Windows error code from GetLastError()\n\nReturns:\n- void (sets TLS errno field as side effect)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xD (13): EACCES - Permission denied\n- 0x8 (8): ENOEXEC - Exec format error\n- 0x16 (22): EINVAL - Invalid argument\n- 0x13-0x24: ERROR_WRITE_PROTECT through ERROR_SHARING_BUFFER_EXCEEDED\n- 0xBC-0xCA: ERROR_INVALID_STARTING_CODESEG through ERROR_INFLOOP_IN_RELOC_CHAIN",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
